course: dictionary
lesson: 10994
title: Describing words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what something looks or feels like. «Toads have dry, warty skin and short legs for walking.» Warty is a describing word, an adjective, and it tells you what the toad's skin is like.
explain: Look at the clues around the word: a toad, dry skin, walking. Warty means covered with warts, small hard lumps on the skin. Picture it in your head: the skin is bumpy and lumpy, not smooth.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Toads have dry, lumpy skin» still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
fact: Warty means covered with warts, small hard lumps on the skin.
fact: «Warty» can also describe any surface that is lumpy and bumpy, like warts.
fact: In nature lessons, toads are often described as warty.
fact: Some animals and plants have warty skin to look less tasty or to hide.
fact: In stories, witches and goblins are sometimes given warty noses.
exercise: «Toads have dry, warty skin and short legs for walking.» What does warty mean? | *Covered with warts, small hard lumps on the skin | Coloured bright green | Wet and slippery all over | Smooth and shiny like glass
exercise: A goblin in a story has a warty nose. What does this suggest? | Its nose is made of glass | Its nose smells of roses | *Its nose is lumpy and bumpy | Its nose is smooth and perfect
exercise: Which of these could be described as warty? | A polished silver spoon | A clean white sheet | A smooth glass marble | *A tree trunk covered in lumps
test: The toad sat on a wet stone with ___ skin on its back. | *Warty | Silky | Smooth and shiny | Sparkly
test: The witch had a long, ___ nose and a crooked hat. | Tiny | Shiny like a mirror | *Warty | Pink and soft
exam: Which phrase best describes a warty toad? | Tall and thin | Smooth and bright | *Covered with small hard lumps like warts | Fast and fierce
